            <ArticleTitle>Premature Growth Plate Closure in a Ballet Dancer en Pointe.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e69-e71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/JSM.0000000000000380</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year-old ballet dancer who had been dancing en pointe (on the tips of the toes) since 10 years presented to the clinic with a shortened right second toe. She had no previous history of pain or trauma. She was diagnosed with premature growth arrest of the second metatarsal head physes resulting in a shortened metatarsal. This is the first reported case of premature growth arrest in a ballet dancer as a result of dancing en pointe.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
